1
00:00:00,387 --> 00:00:02,073
Enjoy!

2
00:00:08,488 --> 00:00:09,570
This is a holdup!

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:11,182
A holdup!

4
00:00:11,207 --> 00:00:12,793
Wait… a holdup?

5
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:14,421
Why?

6
00:00:14,825 --> 00:00:19,253
Ah… I just want to eat at the
restaurant. I don’t have money.

7
00:00:19,278 --> 00:00:21,411
- Oh, is that so?
- Yes.

8
00:00:21,817 --> 00:00:23,503
- Then just eat here…
- Where?

9
00:00:23,922 --> 00:00:26,722
- Here at Bake Haus of U!
- Wow!

10
00:00:26,850 --> 00:00:31,725
The old bakery now serves
short orders too! Right?!

11
00:00:31,750 --> 00:00:31,976
Yes!

12
00:00:32,001 --> 00:00:33,676
The food here is great! What do you want?!

13
00:00:33,701 --> 00:00:34,625
Legit!

14
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:38,397
We’ve got pancit, chicken wings, and more!

15
00:00:38,577 --> 00:00:39,982
And not only is it delicious –

16
00:00:41,304 --> 00:00:44,531
It’s filling at a price that won’t rob you!

17
00:00:45,332 --> 00:00:47,725
- Cut, cut, cut, cut, cut!
- Why?!

18
00:00:48,204 --> 00:00:52,444
Tash, Andres, come on! Fix your acting!

19
00:00:52,577 --> 00:00:53,930
I thought we were doing great…

20
00:00:53,955 --> 00:00:56,354
- Yeah, we were acting…
- Well, they were the ones…

21
00:00:56,971 --> 00:01:01,581
Whoa! Looks like you guys
are shooting a commercial, huh?

22
00:01:01,606 --> 00:01:02,168
Yes!

23
00:01:02,193 --> 00:01:03,727
Yeah, right, Kuya Iskineport!

24
00:01:03,752 --> 00:01:05,213
You were great there, Iskineport!

25
00:01:05,238 --> 00:01:09,501
Since we’ve rebranded the
bakery and added short orders,

26
00:01:09,538 --> 00:01:13,431
we’re also planning to revive the
social media accounts of Bake Haus of U!

27
00:01:13,456 --> 00:01:15,275
- Wow, how fabulous!
- Okay, nice!

28
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:18,423
And our goal is to reach
one million followers!

29
00:01:18,448 --> 00:01:20,589
- One million followers?!
- Yes!

30
00:01:20,734 --> 00:01:25,734
That’s a great idea, but your
commercials—your acting—

31
00:01:26,622 --> 00:01:27,449
should be top-notch!c

32
00:01:27,474 --> 00:01:28,229
It should feel real!

33
00:01:28,254 --> 00:01:29,952
You guys should’ve attended a workshop!

34
00:01:30,284 --> 00:01:31,092
Ah…

35
00:01:31,117 --> 00:01:34,137
Do you have another ski mask?

36
00:01:34,162 --> 00:01:34,731
Ski mask?

37
00:01:34,756 --> 00:01:38,663
You know, this ski mask—just so you know…

38
00:01:38,688 --> 00:01:39,859
I got fact-checked on that!

39
00:01:39,884 --> 00:01:41,389
…it has to be realistic!

40
00:01:41,414 --> 00:01:42,944
Like a real holdup!

41
00:01:42,969 --> 00:01:44,175
This is a holdup!

42
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,408
Nobody move!

43
00:01:45,433 --> 00:01:46,496
No one—

44
00:01:46,521 --> 00:01:47,764
A hold-upper!

45
00:01:47,789 --> 00:01:49,942
Help, neighbors!

46
00:01:49,967 --> 00:01:52,657
Holdup! Holdup! Holdup!

47
00:01:53,919 --> 00:01:56,745
Get him! Punch him!

48
00:01:56,770 --> 00:01:57,875
Holdup!

49
00:03:18,827 --> 00:03:19,980
Hi, Dad!

50
00:03:22,073 --> 00:03:23,726
How are you? Are you okay?

51
00:03:24,685 --> 00:03:25,505
I am okay.

52
00:03:26,411 --> 00:03:29,831
Kuya Andres and I have an idea.

53
00:03:30,165 --> 00:03:37,206
Instead of just taking orders over
the phone, what if we go online?

54
00:03:37,300 --> 00:03:40,300
Because, you know, Gen Z—

55
00:03:40,325 --> 00:03:41,043
Okay!

56
00:03:41,068 --> 00:03:41,614
Hmmm!

57
00:03:41,639 --> 00:03:44,046
No. Don’t.

58
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:45,592
That won’t work.

59
00:03:45,968 --> 00:03:47,441
Just keep it simple—

60
00:03:47,718 --> 00:03:52,097
let’s focus on making our food even
better, and more customers will come.

61
00:03:52,194 --> 00:03:55,668
We don’t need all that delivery stuff!

62
00:03:55,693 --> 00:03:56,308
Wow!

63
00:03:56,567 --> 00:03:58,207
Hater much, my love?

64
00:03:58,495 --> 00:04:00,861
We can do both!

65
00:04:00,886 --> 00:04:04,914
We can improve the food and expand!

66
00:04:05,608 --> 00:04:07,241
No way!

67
00:04:07,266 --> 00:04:10,256
That internet stuff won’t work!

68
00:04:10,281 --> 00:04:12,105
Haven’t you heard?

69
00:04:12,358 --> 00:04:13,638
That’s where all the scams happen!

70
00:04:14,055 --> 00:04:16,448
And you! All your little secrets?
They all come from the internet!

71
00:04:16,473 --> 00:04:18,370
- Whoa… Dad, Dad, Dad.
- I don’t have any secrets, Dad!

72
00:04:18,395 --> 00:04:20,042
- Dad, dad, dad!
- Come on!

73
00:04:20,079 --> 00:04:21,779
- Seriously, Kuya Andres!
- Don’t worry!

74
00:04:21,890 --> 00:04:23,523
We got this, okay?

75
00:04:23,738 --> 00:04:25,665
How can I not worry about you?

76
00:04:25,690 --> 00:04:27,367
Every time I say something,
you get caught up in something!

77
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:28,112
Come on!

78
00:04:28,137 --> 00:04:30,099
And you! You’ve had so many issues already!

79
00:04:30,319 --> 00:04:33,072
Dad, do you know the
saying “happy wife, happy life”?

80
00:04:33,097 --> 00:04:33,632
Oh!

81
00:04:33,657 --> 00:04:36,844
- Exactly! So?!
- Oh? That’s for wives!

82
00:04:37,548 --> 00:04:40,181
Happy kids, happy life!

83
00:04:40,254 --> 00:04:41,300
Yes!

84
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,627
Hey!

85
00:04:46,910 --> 00:04:47,916
That’s right.

86
00:04:48,563 --> 00:04:51,784
You need to be open-minded
about business, like me!

87
00:04:51,809 --> 00:04:56,390
BFF, you seem to be in
a really good mood today!

88
00:04:56,452 --> 00:04:57,152
Not really!

89
00:04:57,177 --> 00:05:00,911
But of course, you’re not the only
ones who can expand a business!

90
00:05:00,936 --> 00:05:02,375
- Oh?
- Of course, I can too!

91
00:05:02,971 --> 00:05:05,443
Wait, so what’s this new business, Karl?

92
00:05:05,468 --> 00:05:08,260
Think of it as a business that’s so me!

93
00:05:08,759 --> 00:05:10,979
I know what it is!

94
00:05:11,004 --> 00:05:12,384
- It has to be totally me!
- Wait a sec!

95
00:05:12,409 --> 00:05:13,448
I know it.

96
00:05:13,606 --> 00:05:15,320
A thrift shop? Perfumes?

97
00:05:16,186 --> 00:05:17,099
No.

98
00:05:17,124 --> 00:05:18,015
No?

99
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:22,047
Come on, it has to be
something that screams me!

100
00:05:22,438 --> 00:05:23,367
A salon?

101
00:05:23,392 --> 00:05:24,685
Manicure-pedicure!

102
00:05:25,583 --> 00:05:28,466
- Wait a minute!
- Oh, oh! Why?! That suits you!

103
00:05:28,491 --> 00:05:30,868
No! I’m a guy! Manicure-pedicure?!

104
00:05:30,912 --> 00:05:31,658
- What?!
- Huh?!

105
00:05:31,683 --> 00:05:32,145
Can I—

106
00:05:32,170 --> 00:05:34,372
- Don’t piss me off!
- So, what is it then?!

107
00:05:34,397 --> 00:05:36,195
- Can you repeat that?
- Yeah, Uncle!

108
00:05:36,395 --> 00:05:42,540
I have a new business—it’s all
about health and wellness spa.

109
00:05:42,565 --> 00:05:44,020
- Ooooh!
- A spa?

110
00:05:44,045 --> 00:05:45,243
You know what, Karl?

111
00:05:45,355 --> 00:05:47,215
That’s totally you!

112
00:05:47,517 --> 00:05:48,605
Of course!

113
00:05:49,522 --> 00:05:51,429
- Here, hold this for me, Andres!
- Okay, sure, sure!

114
00:05:53,823 --> 00:05:58,168
I named it Spakarl Wellness Club!

115
00:05:58,493 --> 00:06:01,340
See?! It’s so me!

116
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:04,007
It suits you, Karl!

117
00:06:04,032 --> 00:06:04,815
Right!

118
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:06,093
- It really does!
- BFF!

119
00:06:06,118 --> 00:06:07,183
Why do you look like that?

120
00:06:07,208 --> 00:06:09,113
Are you sure about that name?

121
00:06:09,262 --> 00:06:10,285
Yes!

122
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:13,109
I already registered
it, so it’s good to go!

123
00:06:13,134 --> 00:06:17,371
And of course, you’re asking
why I chose this business?

124
00:06:17,571 --> 00:06:20,183
Because the owner is very fit!

125
00:06:20,958 --> 00:06:22,111
You know, fit!

126
00:06:22,277 --> 00:06:23,519
Not feet, okay! Fit!

127
00:06:24,454 --> 00:06:27,143
You can tell just by
looking at me—this kind

128
00:06:27,167 --> 00:06:29,855
of business is perfect
for someone like me!

129
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:32,990
Just look at my muscles! Oh!

130
00:06:33,530 --> 00:06:36,788
Check this out! And this!

131
00:06:38,441 --> 00:06:41,547
Rock solid! And this!

132
00:06:41,572 --> 00:06:42,394
- Oh!
- Op!

133
00:06:43,808 --> 00:06:44,595
And then?

134
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:45,888
BFF, what happened?

135
00:06:46,036 --> 00:06:48,623
- Why do you look like—
- I got a cramp.

136
00:06:48,648 --> 00:06:49,276
Huh?!

137
00:06:49,460 --> 00:06:50,680
My knee locked up.

138
00:06:50,705 --> 00:06:51,120
What?!

139
00:06:52,518 --> 00:06:54,572
Are you gonna help me?! No!

140
00:06:54,752 --> 00:06:57,025
Even like this, I can still carry you!

141
00:06:57,050 --> 00:06:57,545
Really?!

142
00:06:57,598 --> 00:07:00,064
Oh, as long as I have
my business, I’m happy.

143
00:07:00,799 --> 00:07:01,946
You okay, Karl?!

144
00:07:01,971 --> 00:07:02,879
Don’t cause a commotion!

145
00:07:02,904 --> 00:07:04,330
- Karl!
- I got this!

146
00:07:04,355 --> 00:07:06,933
- Karl! BFF! You okay?
- I can handle myself!

147
00:07:08,061 --> 00:07:09,548
Karl!

148
00:07:10,981 --> 00:07:12,081
That looked painful!

149
00:07:15,006 --> 00:07:19,102
Are you sure you want to
apply as a manager here?!

150
00:07:21,266 --> 00:07:23,766
I’m not looking for a masseur!

151
00:07:23,791 --> 00:07:25,287
I’m good at giving massages!

152
00:07:25,312 --> 00:07:25,779
Massage?

153
00:07:25,804 --> 00:07:27,280
We always give massages at home.

154
00:07:27,351 --> 00:07:30,315
Never mind, I’ll just call
you… is your number here?

155
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:32,221
I’ll just call you if I need someone.

156
00:07:32,246 --> 00:07:34,284
If you ever get injured, sir, call me.

157
00:07:34,309 --> 00:07:36,562
Uh, don’t wish that on me!

158
00:07:36,587 --> 00:07:38,627
I don’t want to
end up owing you!

159
00:07:39,783 --> 00:07:42,243
Are you selling jewelry here too?!

160
00:07:45,605 --> 00:07:46,612
Buffet?

161
00:07:48,106 --> 00:07:50,046
Do you even know what you’re applying for?

162
00:07:50,129 --> 00:07:51,955
Why do you want to be a masseur?

163
00:07:54,448 --> 00:07:55,479
Oh no!

164
00:07:56,033 --> 00:07:58,157
You have no experience in massage!

165
00:07:58,182 --> 00:08:00,677
Do you even know how to do it?!

166
00:08:01,430 --> 00:08:02,990
Are your past clients still alive?

167
00:08:05,023 --> 00:08:05,623
See!

168
00:08:05,648 --> 00:08:11,286
I’ll call you if needed, okay?

169
00:08:11,498 --> 00:08:12,690
Leave your number.

170
00:08:15,439 --> 00:08:16,539
Hit the gym!

171
00:08:26,150 --> 00:08:27,307
Can you handle it?!

172
00:08:28,580 --> 00:08:29,643
I still can.

173
00:08:29,909 --> 00:08:32,082
Actually, you might not
know this, but I go to the gym.

174
00:08:32,210 --> 00:08:33,377
You work out?

175
00:08:33,958 --> 00:08:35,502
No, I’m serious. Can you really do it?

176
00:08:35,549 --> 00:08:36,049
I still can.

177
00:08:36,095 --> 00:08:37,422
Is your number here?

178
00:08:38,181 --> 00:08:39,215
This one, this one, this one.

179
00:08:39,456 --> 00:08:40,650
Never mind, I’ll call you.

180
00:08:40,675 --> 00:08:43,189
But my advice? Take vitamins!

181
00:08:43,879 --> 00:08:44,905
You can do it!

182
00:08:45,283 --> 00:08:48,329
You need strength.

183
00:08:48,749 --> 00:08:52,985
Being a masseur is tough work.

184
00:08:53,010 --> 00:08:54,026
I’ll call you!

185
00:08:54,228 --> 00:08:56,152
- Yes. Thank you.
- Thank you.

186
00:08:56,258 --> 00:08:57,338
Be safe.

187
00:09:05,531 --> 00:09:08,857
Hmm! This one might be okay!

188
00:09:11,438 --> 00:09:12,487
Can I see?

189
00:09:14,782 --> 00:09:15,962
You look like…

190
00:09:20,246 --> 00:09:21,682
do you have experience?

191
00:09:22,168 --> 00:09:30,257
Do you have any experience in massaging,
or managing a spa or wellness center?

192
00:09:30,282 --> 00:09:31,495
Do you have any experience?

193
00:09:32,316 --> 00:09:35,249
No, but… I’m really good at grinding.

194
00:09:36,449 --> 00:09:37,495
Grinding?

195
00:09:38,038 --> 00:09:39,065
Hey!

196
00:09:40,027 --> 00:09:41,020
What?!

197
00:09:41,045 --> 00:09:43,144
Why are you saying
things like that?!

198
00:09:44,630 --> 00:09:45,643
What’s that?!

199
00:09:46,477 --> 00:09:47,703
What’s that supposed to mean?!

200
00:09:47,728 --> 00:09:49,796
That’s not allowed!

201
00:09:50,626 --> 00:09:54,716
It’s a massage business!
You’ll be managing everything!

202
00:09:54,741 --> 00:09:56,556
I need someone trustworthy!

203
00:09:56,649 --> 00:09:59,322
How can I trust you if
you’re saying things like that?!

204
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:01,761
That’s not okay!

205
00:10:02,951 --> 00:10:05,111
There are still
opportunities, don’t worry.

206
00:10:08,114 --> 00:10:09,821
You still have a chance.

207
00:10:10,063 --> 00:10:12,123
You will not lose a job.

208
00:10:12,155 --> 00:10:13,322
I’ll call you, alright?

209
00:10:13,347 --> 00:10:14,496
It's okay.

210
00:10:14,521 --> 00:10:16,288
- My number is there.
- Yeah, I see it.

211
00:10:16,313 --> 00:10:17,110
Alright.

212
00:10:17,135 --> 00:10:18,289
I’ll call you! Yes.

213
00:10:18,314 --> 00:10:19,665
Good. Sorry, okay?

214
00:10:19,862 --> 00:10:21,382
You’re not fit for management.

215
00:10:23,091 --> 00:10:24,184
What is going on?!

216
00:10:25,790 --> 00:10:27,936
So many weirdos!

217
00:10:28,164 --> 00:10:29,597
Why are you here?!

218
00:10:29,622 --> 00:10:32,368
Hi, Tso K! Isn’t it obvious?

219
00:10:32,393 --> 00:10:37,792
I’m applying for the
managerial position at SpaKarl!

220
00:10:37,817 --> 00:10:42,220
And next, I’ll apply for your heart!

221
00:10:42,347 --> 00:10:43,620
Wait a minute!

222
00:10:43,753 --> 00:10:45,973
Don’t you have a
cellphone business?

223
00:10:46,150 --> 00:10:49,350
Ah, the cell—yeah, that’s fine!

224
00:10:49,375 --> 00:10:51,995
My relatives can manage that!

225
00:10:52,043 --> 00:10:55,190
But this one—I really want to be a manager!

226
00:10:55,215 --> 00:10:59,277
And you know I’m a
Zumba instructor! Hey, hey!

227
00:10:59,615 --> 00:11:00,229
Okay!

228
00:11:01,390 --> 00:11:02,164
But no!

229
00:11:02,856 --> 00:11:07,236
I don’t want to hire someone I know.

230
00:11:07,874 --> 00:11:10,801
Business is business.

231
00:11:11,171 --> 00:11:13,251
I need someone I don’t know.

232
00:11:13,726 --> 00:11:18,059
Sorry, Mariposa. You’re confusing me.

233
00:11:18,256 --> 00:11:19,630
You’ll change your mind.

234
00:11:21,615 --> 00:11:23,188
She could be a good fit, but so persistent!

235
00:11:24,185 --> 00:11:26,152
Is there no one else applying?

236
00:11:44,090 --> 00:11:45,122
Me.

237
00:11:50,870 --> 00:11:51,918
You?

238
00:12:06,073 --> 00:12:07,121
Name?

239
00:12:08,351 --> 00:12:12,017
My name is Valerie…

240
00:12:14,543 --> 00:12:16,789
Valderama.

241
00:12:19,105 --> 00:12:21,579
Valerie Valderama.

242
00:12:23,305 --> 00:12:24,332
Wow!

243
00:12:25,091 --> 00:12:26,137
That tickled me.

244
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:27,895
This one seems okay.

245
00:12:29,464 --> 00:12:32,544
Your lady for the night.

246
00:12:32,989 --> 00:12:34,114
Whoa!

247
00:12:37,734 --> 00:12:38,800
She’s used to this!

248
00:12:39,557 --> 00:12:41,457
This is great! And she’s pretty!

249
00:12:42,130 --> 00:12:43,207
Nice.

250
00:12:43,294 --> 00:12:44,574
- Nice?
- Yes.

251
00:12:46,767 --> 00:12:47,903
Very fit!

252
00:12:52,199 --> 00:12:53,259
Vavavoom!

253
00:12:58,190 --> 00:12:59,247
Oh no!

254
00:13:00,263 --> 00:13:01,434
This is bad!

255
00:13:03,368 --> 00:13:06,258
Here are the chicken
wings you ordered! Enjoy!

256
00:13:06,483 --> 00:13:07,555
Thank you!

257
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:09,067
Please visit us again!

258
00:13:09,889 --> 00:13:10,949
So fun! Is it okay?

259
00:13:11,508 --> 00:13:12,548
You guys need anything?

260
00:13:13,134 --> 00:13:14,148
All good?

261
00:13:14,799 --> 00:13:16,554
And you, can I take your order?

262
00:13:17,180 --> 00:13:18,301
What would you like?

263
00:13:18,326 --> 00:13:20,239
- Tash, Tash! Look at this!
- Sorry…

264
00:13:20,705 --> 00:13:23,552
We got our first online
order! Look at that!

265
00:13:23,885 --> 00:13:24,452
Right?!

266
00:13:24,482 --> 00:13:27,735
Okay, let’s go, let’s go! Where are
Kuya Iskineport and Kuya Chard?

267
00:13:28,141 --> 00:13:28,781
I have no idea!

268
00:13:28,806 --> 00:13:30,106
- Tash!
- Hey, Tash!

269
00:13:30,131 --> 00:13:33,037
Andres! We had an accident!

270
00:13:34,743 --> 00:13:37,690
We saw the su— No, we skidded!

271
00:13:38,133 --> 00:13:43,014
Yeah, and we can’t
deliver your bread for now.

272
00:13:43,059 --> 00:13:46,062
Oh no, that’s okay. Just rest, alright?

273
00:13:46,087 --> 00:13:47,168
Take it easy.

274
00:13:47,193 --> 00:13:48,108
Yeah.

275
00:13:48,133 --> 00:13:49,326
What do we do now?

276
00:13:51,698 --> 00:13:55,675
I don’t know. But, Tash, Mom
and Dad can’t find out about this.

277
00:13:57,534 --> 00:13:59,154
And we can’t fail, Tash.

278
00:13:59,502 --> 00:14:00,729
So we have no choice.

279
00:14:01,486 --> 00:14:04,112
We have to do the
deliveries ourselves. Right?

280
00:14:04,343 --> 00:14:06,136
Where are the motorcycle keys?

281
00:14:06,175 --> 00:14:09,200
You two take so long to talk,
and we’re the ones with disabilities!

282
00:14:09,225 --> 00:14:12,839
Well, where are the
keys?! We need them now!

283
00:14:12,923 --> 00:14:14,197
Ah, ouch!

284
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:16,914
He has them! He has them!

285
00:14:16,967 --> 00:14:18,101
It’s scratched!

286
00:14:18,126 --> 00:14:21,946
You even peeled the wound—put
it back! Will a key fit in a wound?

287
00:14:21,971 --> 00:14:24,278
- Would it even fit?
- Oh, sorry, sorry, I just need the key.

288
00:14:28,942 --> 00:14:30,949
Thank you so much, Lola Maxi.

289
00:14:30,974 --> 00:14:32,662
I’m glad you came with me.

290
00:14:32,999 --> 00:14:36,713
Andres will handle the far orders,
and I’ll take care of the nearby ones.

291
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:39,233
Oh, don’t worry!

292
00:14:39,384 --> 00:14:42,477
This place is super close
to us, just walking distance!

293
00:14:42,502 --> 00:14:46,536
It’s good for me to
go out once in a while!

294
00:14:48,650 --> 00:14:50,957
Pose and post!

295
00:14:50,982 --> 00:14:54,024
Alright, I’ll just ring the doorbell here.

296
00:14:57,963 --> 00:15:00,589
Here we go! Our first order!

297
00:15:00,955 --> 00:15:03,395
- Are you sure this is the right address?
- Yes! It’s here!

298
00:15:04,294 --> 00:15:05,594
One Lucky Street!

299
00:15:05,619 --> 00:15:08,449
Alright, I’ll show this to Cha and Aga.

300
00:15:08,474 --> 00:15:10,009
Exciting! Okay, let’s take a photo first!

301
00:15:11,559 --> 00:15:13,445
This is correct, right? There!

302
00:15:13,887 --> 00:15:18,332
Hello! Your order from Bake Haus of U!

303
00:15:21,394 --> 00:15:24,897
- Here’s your delivery.
- Honey, the delivery guy’s here!

304
00:15:25,595 --> 00:15:27,575
- Here you go.
- Okay, hold on. I’ll just get the payment.

305
00:15:33,386 --> 00:15:35,826
Her tumor is so big, poor old lady.

306
00:15:35,851 --> 00:15:36,900
Huh?!

307
00:15:36,925 --> 00:15:38,265
Hello! How are you?

308
00:15:38,569 --> 00:15:40,669
You’re such an idiot, darling!

309
00:15:41,330 --> 00:15:42,824
You’re deaf!

310
00:15:43,156 --> 00:15:47,236
I didn’t tell you to order food!

311
00:15:47,261 --> 00:15:53,028
I said to call the
baby delivery guy!

312
00:15:53,059 --> 00:15:54,145
- Kuya?
- Yes?

313
00:15:54,170 --> 00:15:56,542
- Is that your wife?
- Yes, she’s my wife.

314
00:15:57,072 --> 00:15:59,439
Oh… how old is she?

315
00:15:59,464 --> 00:16:01,184
- Seventy-eight. She’s seventy-eight.
- Huh?!

316
00:16:01,209 --> 00:16:02,263
Yes.

317
00:16:03,229 --> 00:16:04,229
Hold on!

318
00:16:05,336 --> 00:16:07,656
We might still catch them here!

319
00:16:07,681 --> 00:16:09,704
- No! Not here!
- Wait! Wait!

320
00:16:14,070 --> 00:16:16,537
That’s fine. Look at your resume.

321
00:16:16,562 --> 00:16:21,153
But Valerie, I still need
to interview you, okay?

322
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:25,806
So, what do you think
you can offer SpaKarl?

323
00:16:26,556 --> 00:16:30,883
First of all, I have a beauty—right, boys?!

324
00:16:30,908 --> 00:16:33,619
- Yes! Yes! That’s right!
- Hey!

325
00:16:35,019 --> 00:16:36,659
Valerie beauty!

326
00:16:37,096 --> 00:16:38,249
What are you all doing here?!

327
00:16:38,274 --> 00:16:39,493
Why is everyone here?!

328
00:16:39,518 --> 00:16:41,037
Stop it, this isn’t a tournament!

329
00:16:41,577 --> 00:16:44,342
And you’re all crammed in here!

330
00:16:45,141 --> 00:16:46,735
Oh, you too?

331
00:16:47,459 --> 00:16:49,113
Weren’t you in an
accident earlier?

332
00:16:49,199 --> 00:16:50,605
Ah, the doctor was amazing.

333
00:16:50,663 --> 00:16:51,830
He treated us right away.

334
00:16:51,855 --> 00:16:55,446
He told us to come back
here for a consultation… for you.

335
00:16:55,471 --> 00:16:56,786
Yes… Tso K.

336
00:16:56,811 --> 00:17:00,563
That was fast! You want
me to add more bandages?

337
00:17:00,588 --> 00:17:02,128
No need, Tso K! I’m good.

338
00:17:02,153 --> 00:17:03,228
You’re something else!

339
00:17:03,253 --> 00:17:04,281
I’ll get back to you later.

340
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:05,907
Valerie, let’s continue.

341
00:17:06,347 --> 00:17:08,560
What are your specialties?

342
00:17:09,397 --> 00:17:11,450
I have a lot of experience, Boss Tso K.

343
00:17:12,232 --> 00:17:13,625
I know yoga…

344
00:17:13,665 --> 00:17:15,704
Oh! Yoga!

345
00:17:16,884 --> 00:17:18,444
I can be a cowboy!

346
00:17:20,894 --> 00:17:23,647
I know the countdown dog!

347
00:17:25,932 --> 00:17:28,852
Just hire her, Tso K! Hire her!

348
00:17:28,877 --> 00:17:30,443
- What are you waiting for?!
- She’s smart, she’s smart!

349
00:17:30,468 --> 00:17:31,867
Why are you all interfering?!

350
00:17:32,473 --> 00:17:33,939
Are you the ones making
the decisions here?!

351
00:17:34,192 --> 00:17:36,398
Why are you telling me
whether to hire her or not?!

352
00:17:36,523 --> 00:17:37,949
- Ah…
- Sorry, Tso K.

353
00:17:38,831 --> 00:17:42,191
Boss Tso K, they’re all
signing up for memberships.

354
00:17:42,756 --> 00:17:44,163
They’re customers too!

355
00:17:45,287 --> 00:17:46,647
Right, boys?!

356
00:17:50,264 --> 00:17:53,298
One more thing! If you
don’t shut up, I’ll hit you all!

357
00:17:55,696 --> 00:17:56,976
And here’s the kicker!

358
00:17:57,001 --> 00:17:59,352
Hey, hey, hey!

359
00:17:59,443 --> 00:18:06,237
We’re going to make the cripple walk!

360
00:18:09,275 --> 00:18:10,030
Hey!

361
00:18:10,055 --> 00:18:11,648
I can walk now, Tso K!

362
00:18:11,673 --> 00:18:12,853
Look!

363
00:18:13,065 --> 00:18:14,478
I can even dance!

364
00:18:14,658 --> 00:18:15,397
A miracle!

365
00:18:15,422 --> 00:18:18,328
He can walk!

366
00:18:18,512 --> 00:18:20,119
But now he can’t go home!

367
00:18:21,958 --> 00:18:24,990
Oh! He’s still crippled! I
really thought it was a miracle!

368
00:18:25,015 --> 00:18:26,204
Just do it, Iskineport!

369
00:18:26,229 --> 00:18:27,368
No, I’m really crippled.

370
00:18:27,393 --> 00:18:28,859
- Huh?
- I’m just crippled.

371
00:18:28,884 --> 00:18:30,825
But I think I went blind too!

372
00:18:34,404 --> 00:18:41,816
Anyway, Valerie, for me, your
resume looks good, so… you’re hired!

373
00:18:45,284 --> 00:18:46,738
Valerie!

374
00:18:46,763 --> 00:18:48,337
Valerie!

375
00:18:48,362 --> 00:18:49,779
Valerie!

376
00:18:49,804 --> 00:18:52,116
We’re signing up as members now!

377
00:19:02,693 --> 00:19:03,934
Anne, hey!

378
00:19:03,959 --> 00:19:05,114
Wake up!

379
00:19:06,698 --> 00:19:07,465
Hey! Anne!

380
00:19:07,490 --> 00:19:08,453
Wake up!

381
00:19:08,478 --> 00:19:10,164
- Sorry!
- We’re here!

382
00:19:10,324 --> 00:19:11,513
Oh, we’re here already?

383
00:19:13,514 --> 00:19:14,802
Alright.

384
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:16,685
You okay?

385
00:19:18,197 --> 00:19:20,163
Thanks for coming with me.

386
00:19:21,009 --> 00:19:22,576
Good thing Tso K agreed, right?

387
00:19:22,767 --> 00:19:23,807
Of course!

388
00:19:24,375 --> 00:19:25,588
And besides, he’s busy.

389
00:19:25,888 --> 00:19:26,760
Don’t worry.

390
00:19:26,785 --> 00:19:30,445
He didn’t want to be interviewed because
he’s the one doing interviews at the spa.

391
00:19:30,470 --> 00:19:31,567
At the spa?

392
00:19:31,951 --> 00:19:33,231
Ah, okay. That
makes sense. Okay.

393
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:34,997
Where’s the house?

394
00:19:35,150 --> 00:19:36,275
- Here it is!
- This one? This one?

395
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:38,347
02 Acacia Drive.

396
00:19:38,886 --> 00:19:39,888
Okay.

397
00:19:44,173 --> 00:19:45,220
Hello?

398
00:19:48,450 --> 00:19:49,692
Hello!

399
00:19:49,717 --> 00:19:50,850
Anybody home?

400
00:19:53,207 --> 00:19:54,315
What do you think, Anne?

401
00:19:54,340 --> 00:19:55,485
Just call them.

402
00:19:57,343 --> 00:19:58,493
Wait a second.

403
00:20:03,997 --> 00:20:05,215
They’re not answering?

404
00:20:06,045 --> 00:20:07,356
Nope, no answer.

405
00:20:08,525 --> 00:20:09,582
Now what?

406
00:20:17,468 --> 00:20:20,105
You! You’ve been
lying to me for so long!

407
00:20:20,130 --> 00:20:21,412
I’m going to kill you!

408
00:20:21,996 --> 00:20:23,136
I’m going to kill you!

409
00:20:26,290 --> 00:20:27,797
You’ve been lying to me for so long!

410
00:20:28,701 --> 00:20:30,594
Oh, that looks safe!

411
00:20:30,619 --> 00:20:31,760
Let’s go!

412
00:20:33,539 --> 00:20:35,246
Hey, wait, why are you driving?!

413
00:20:36,285 --> 00:20:37,152
Let’s go!

414
00:20:37,303 --> 00:20:41,408
Kuya Andres, our
delivery earlier was a mess.

415
00:20:42,085 --> 00:20:44,685
With everything that happened,
we didn’t even get paid.

416
00:20:45,978 --> 00:20:47,078
Ours was even worse.

417
00:20:49,928 --> 00:20:51,608
Tasha! Andres!

418
00:20:51,633 --> 00:20:52,716
Good news!

419
00:20:52,741 --> 00:20:53,532
Look at this!

420
00:20:53,557 --> 00:21:00,813
I’ve been tracking our orders, and we just
got a big one worth five thousand pesos!

421
00:21:01,200 --> 00:21:03,427
But… it’s cash on delivery.

422
00:21:03,452 --> 00:21:04,483
Huh?

423
00:21:04,946 --> 00:21:06,279
Are we really
gonna risk it, Kuya?

424
00:21:07,660 --> 00:21:08,674
I think we should!

425
00:21:08,699 --> 00:21:12,541
This might be our chance to at least
recover some of our capital, right?

426
00:21:12,725 --> 00:21:15,485
Oh, kids, don’t worry.

427
00:21:15,510 --> 00:21:19,402
Look at this, we got a great review!

428
00:21:19,601 --> 00:21:20,675
Five stars!

429
00:21:20,967 --> 00:21:22,834
I’ll read it out loud!

430
00:21:22,875 --> 00:21:28,205
"Lola Maxi is great at
delivering babies!" See?

431
00:21:28,230 --> 00:21:30,212
Mom, that’s not about the food.

432
00:21:30,764 --> 00:21:32,478
Oh, don’t worry!

433
00:21:32,503 --> 00:21:39,042
More customers will come,
and we’ll get even better reviews.

434
00:21:40,102 --> 00:21:41,344
Don’t stress!

435
00:21:44,245 --> 00:21:45,512
- Ah, Tso K…
- Yeah?

436
00:21:45,537 --> 00:21:46,503
My membership?

437
00:21:47,083 --> 00:21:48,164
Okay!

438
00:21:49,770 --> 00:21:52,177
Hmm… hey, this is too much.

439
00:21:52,327 --> 00:21:53,660
There’s an extra five hundred here!

440
00:21:53,758 --> 00:21:55,251
I gave extra on purpose.

441
00:21:55,557 --> 00:21:57,324
One of them is for Valerie.

442
00:21:57,687 --> 00:21:58,357
Whoa!

443
00:21:58,382 --> 00:21:59,335
Wow!

444
00:21:59,916 --> 00:22:01,070
Dang, that look could kill!

445
00:22:01,600 --> 00:22:03,479
Hey, someone’s waiting behind you!

446
00:22:03,504 --> 00:22:04,572
- All good now?
- All good.

447
00:22:04,597 --> 00:22:05,554
Okay, thank you!

448
00:22:05,579 --> 00:22:07,865
- Oh, that five hundred is for you.
- Bye!

449
00:22:09,098 --> 00:22:10,146
How much?

450
00:22:10,179 --> 00:22:10,857
One five.

451
00:22:10,882 --> 00:22:11,382
One five?

452
00:22:11,407 --> 00:22:12,960
Hey! Hey, hey, hey!

453
00:22:13,015 --> 00:22:14,849
So, you two are just here!

454
00:22:15,365 --> 00:22:16,998
I was looking for you!

455
00:22:17,023 --> 00:22:20,165
We’re just resting, Kuya
Aga, because we’re injured!

456
00:22:20,190 --> 00:22:23,151
Give us a break! We
can’t work at the bakery!

457
00:22:25,503 --> 00:22:28,257
Hi, Sir! My name is Valerie.

458
00:22:28,919 --> 00:22:31,545
Would you like to sign up
for a SpaKarl membership?

459
00:22:33,450 --> 00:22:35,030
Oh, wait, wait!

460
00:22:35,173 --> 00:22:39,386
So this is what you
meant by resting?!

461
00:22:39,605 --> 00:22:40,811
This?!

462
00:22:41,568 --> 00:22:43,701
Hold on, hold on. You’re so worked up!

463
00:22:43,827 --> 00:22:45,347
I’m not worked up, I’m just confused.

464
00:22:45,372 --> 00:22:46,469
You have a SpaKarl…

465
00:22:46,549 --> 00:22:48,589
If that’s the case, just close your eyes!

466
00:22:48,829 --> 00:22:49,882
Why close my eyes?

467
00:22:49,907 --> 00:22:51,469
Because if you’re jealous, close your eyes!

468
00:22:52,927 --> 00:22:54,280
So you’re jealous, Kuya Aga!

469
00:22:55,112 --> 00:22:55,730
Tso K!

470
00:22:55,755 --> 00:22:56,143
What?!

471
00:22:56,168 --> 00:22:58,701
Is she the one you
replaced me with?! Is she?!

472
00:22:58,752 --> 00:22:59,827
Is she, huh?!

473
00:22:59,852 --> 00:23:01,953
What do you mean “her”?!
What are you even saying?!

474
00:23:02,704 --> 00:23:04,850
I know Valerie!

475
00:23:05,632 --> 00:23:07,258
She used to be in my Zumba group!

476
00:23:07,283 --> 00:23:07,957
Oh really?!

477
00:23:07,982 --> 00:23:09,575
- She’s a thief!
- Huh?!

478
00:23:09,600 --> 00:23:12,344
- A thief?!
- She’s a fake! Fake!

479
00:23:12,369 --> 00:23:15,278
Hey! Watch what you’re saying!

480
00:23:15,671 --> 00:23:17,644
Maybe your eyes
are the dirty ones, girl!

481
00:23:18,172 --> 00:23:20,609
- Oh! She’s fighting back?!
- Oh, is that how it is?!

482
00:23:21,667 --> 00:23:23,434
Hey, Mariposa! Mariposa!

483
00:23:23,655 --> 00:23:26,349
- Wait, wait, wait!
- What?! What?!

484
00:23:27,738 --> 00:23:28,935
You want to go chest to chest?!

485
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:30,436
Fine, let’s do it!

486
00:23:35,163 --> 00:23:37,923
This is it, the last and
biggest delivery of the day.

487
00:23:38,377 --> 00:23:40,844
No matter who it is, we’re
collecting payment, okay?

488
00:23:41,446 --> 00:23:42,812
Of course, Kuya!

489
00:23:42,837 --> 00:23:44,052
It’s worth five thousand!

490
00:23:44,077 --> 00:23:45,352
We’ll make it all back for Dad!

491
00:23:45,416 --> 00:23:49,446
Once this order is done,
all we have to do is wait!

492
00:23:49,819 --> 00:23:50,392
Okay.

493
00:23:58,592 --> 00:24:00,245
The person who ordered isn’t replying.

494
00:24:00,778 --> 00:24:02,745
What now? Maybe they fell asleep?

495
00:24:02,878 --> 00:24:03,925
Or maybe they’re busy?

496
00:24:05,099 --> 00:24:06,619
Wait, why here?

497
00:24:07,047 --> 00:24:09,700
Maybe they don’t want
to reveal their address?

498
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:10,800
Address reveal?

499
00:24:10,825 --> 00:24:12,281
Yeah, they just pinned this location.

500
00:24:12,306 --> 00:24:13,432
Let’s just wait, okay?

501
00:24:13,457 --> 00:24:14,943
All we have to do is wait.

502
00:24:15,396 --> 00:24:16,303
So, relax.

503
00:24:16,328 --> 00:24:17,309
Okay.

504
00:24:17,334 --> 00:24:18,341
Wait.

505
00:24:47,456 --> 00:24:50,269
Hello? Where are you?
It’s been thirty minutes.

506
00:24:50,787 --> 00:24:52,005
This is taking so long, Tash!

507
00:24:53,715 --> 00:24:54,695
Kuya, they replied!

508
00:24:54,720 --> 00:24:55,833
- They replied?!
- They replied.

509
00:24:55,858 --> 00:24:56,941
Look, look!

510
00:24:57,748 --> 00:25:00,022
"It’s a prank" with a smiley face.

511
00:25:01,301 --> 00:25:02,355
It’s a prank?!

512
00:25:03,434 --> 00:25:04,847
We got scammed?!

513
00:25:07,512 --> 00:25:11,452
Wow, Valerie! You’re amazing!

514
00:25:11,862 --> 00:25:13,861
Imagine, you got all
those guys to sign up for

515
00:25:13,885 --> 00:25:15,883
a membership, and
SpaKarl isn’t even open yet!

516
00:25:16,872 --> 00:25:21,872
Boss K, I’m really sorry
about my fight with Mariposa.

517
00:25:22,019 --> 00:25:24,546
I don’t know what her problem
is—she’s always badmouthing me

518
00:25:24,965 --> 00:25:26,858
when I’m just trying
to work honestly.

519
00:25:27,247 --> 00:25:28,567
Forget about it.

520
00:25:29,023 --> 00:25:31,830
To be honest, she’s totally into me.

521
00:25:32,767 --> 00:25:33,825
Just let it go.

522
00:25:36,404 --> 00:25:41,140
Wait a sec, I need to
grab something inside.

523
00:25:42,898 --> 00:25:43,818
Boss K…

524
00:25:45,031 --> 00:25:45,938
Congrats!

525
00:25:45,963 --> 00:25:47,263
Thanks so much!

526
00:25:47,288 --> 00:25:48,667
I’m so happy, we got
so many new members

527
00:25:48,691 --> 00:25:50,391
again! Hold on, I just
need to get something.

528
00:25:50,416 --> 00:25:51,690
- Go ahead.
- Stay here, okay?

529
00:25:57,686 --> 00:25:58,513
Ouch!

530
00:25:58,835 --> 00:26:00,002
Hey, look! It’s Valerie!

531
00:26:00,027 --> 00:26:00,714
Valerie!

532
00:26:00,739 --> 00:26:05,180
You’re so sexy! You know,
since we’re already members…

533
00:26:05,205 --> 00:26:05,887
Yeah!

534
00:26:05,931 --> 00:26:06,731
…of SpaKarl,

535
00:26:06,756 --> 00:26:10,076
maybe you could give us a
little sample of your services?

536
00:26:10,156 --> 00:26:11,102
Yeah, Valerie!

537
00:26:11,127 --> 00:26:13,425
Maybe you know
some cool techniques!

538
00:26:13,450 --> 00:26:16,823
Like the ones I see on TikTok,
you know, the chiropractor

539
00:26:17,107 --> 00:26:18,754
moves that crack your bones!

540
00:26:20,187 --> 00:26:22,019
- My back is killing me!
- Sure, guys!

541
00:26:23,169 --> 00:26:23,673
She’s coming closer!

542
00:26:23,706 --> 00:26:24,808
But let’s do it tomorrow, okay?

543
00:26:24,833 --> 00:26:26,390
She’s getting closer—I’m freezing up!

544
00:26:26,415 --> 00:26:27,376
- Huh?
- I’m just exhausted from…

545
00:26:27,401 --> 00:26:28,937
Don’t freeze up, you
might have a heart attack!

546
00:26:29,008 --> 00:26:30,594
…getting beaten up
by Mariposa earlier.

547
00:26:30,619 --> 00:26:31,775
Oh yeah, that’s right!

548
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:32,719
Yeah, Mariposa really went too far!

549
00:26:32,744 --> 00:26:34,522
You shouldn’t be messing
around in this place…

550
00:26:34,547 --> 00:26:38,097
Hey, you too?! Oh no, me too!

551
00:26:38,122 --> 00:26:39,715
Sorry, guys, let’s just do it tomorrow!

552
00:26:39,740 --> 00:26:40,687
- Alright.
- Tomorrow?

553
00:26:40,712 --> 00:26:41,705
We’ll be back tomorrow!

554
00:26:41,730 --> 00:26:42,533
Yeah, we’ll be back tomorrow!

555
00:26:42,558 --> 00:26:44,885
- 12:01, we’re here, okay?!
- 12:01, yup! Let’s get here early!

556
00:26:45,345 --> 00:26:47,045
If you want, you can come together.

557
00:26:47,070 --> 00:26:47,672
Together?!

558
00:26:47,697 --> 00:26:48,356
Oh, together!

559
00:26:48,381 --> 00:26:50,602
I’ll hurry up, I won’t even sleep!

560
00:26:50,942 --> 00:26:52,582
We’ll come together! We’ll come together!

561
00:27:04,974 --> 00:27:06,028
Dad was right!

562
00:27:07,297 --> 00:27:09,250
Should we just admit we got scammed?!

563
00:27:09,275 --> 00:27:09,871
What?!

564
00:27:09,896 --> 00:27:12,542
Whoa, whoa, whoa! No,
no, no! That’s scary, Tash.

565
00:27:12,926 --> 00:27:15,799
We need to get rid of this
so there’s no evidence, okay?

566
00:27:16,635 --> 00:27:17,697
Okay!

567
00:27:18,698 --> 00:27:20,878
But we still have to tell the truth.

568
00:27:21,175 --> 00:27:23,502
Let’s not admit it,
okay? Let’s not admit it.

569
00:27:23,527 --> 00:27:27,553
He’s our dad! We’re not supposed to
keep secrets! We’re supposed to be honest—

570
00:27:29,777 --> 00:27:30,777
So...

571
00:27:31,624 --> 00:27:33,744
So, how’s your business?

572
00:27:35,438 --> 00:27:36,632
Your deliveries?

573
00:27:36,657 --> 00:27:37,773
Is that it?

574
00:27:44,137 --> 00:27:45,503
You guys sound all over the place.

575
00:27:45,874 --> 00:27:48,421
See? I told you this would happen, right?

576
00:27:48,784 --> 00:27:52,707
Things went wrong again.

577
00:27:52,732 --> 00:27:56,542
Before you deliver, you should
always make sure you’re paid first.

578
00:27:57,022 --> 00:27:59,282
Then you send out the order.

579
00:28:01,229 --> 00:28:02,916
- Sorry, Dad.
- Sorry, Dad.

580
00:28:03,578 --> 00:28:05,191
My love, relax.

581
00:28:05,395 --> 00:28:09,685
They didn’t mean for this to happen.
And they’ve been working all day.

582
00:28:09,710 --> 00:28:10,863
Look at them, poor things.

583
00:28:10,888 --> 00:28:13,732
Of course! I’m not even
mad, my eyes are just big.

584
00:28:13,757 --> 00:28:16,790
Listen, you two, it’s not a problem for me.

585
00:28:17,815 --> 00:28:22,356
What matters is that I never lose
trust in you when it comes to business

586
00:28:22,381 --> 00:28:25,175
because I know
you gave it your all.

587
00:28:26,180 --> 00:28:28,573
Sometimes, you’ll mess up.
Sometimes, you’ll lose money.

588
00:28:28,912 --> 00:28:31,602
Sometimes, things won’t go your
way. That’s just how business is.

589
00:28:31,978 --> 00:28:39,896
And you’ll meet all sorts of
characters when you run a business.

590
00:28:40,585 --> 00:28:41,771
Look at me!

591
00:28:42,841 --> 00:28:45,648
I’m like a carinderia that’s always open!

592
00:28:45,673 --> 00:28:49,635
- No, no, no, no, no, no! Lola Maxi!
- Where are you going now?!

593
00:28:49,660 --> 00:28:50,510
Yeah, where is she off to this time?!

594
00:28:50,535 --> 00:28:52,179
What do you mean by that, Lola Maxi?

595
00:28:52,204 --> 00:28:54,709
Don’t even try to figure
out what she means!

596
00:28:54,734 --> 00:28:59,983
Let’s just do this instead—let’s
eat! Come on, let’s eat already!

597
00:29:03,897 --> 00:29:08,037
Valerie! I left my keys.

598
00:29:12,365 --> 00:29:17,945
Wait a sec… why do you have the cashbox?

599
00:29:19,481 --> 00:29:23,928
Ouch! Why did you hit me?!

600
00:29:24,227 --> 00:29:25,340
Ugh, Karl!

601
00:29:25,600 --> 00:29:27,673
I wasn’t really planning to hurt you!

602
00:29:28,008 --> 00:29:29,821
Oh yeah? Then why’d you do it?!

603
00:29:30,098 --> 00:29:33,451
Actually, it’s not even
the money I’m after!

604
00:29:33,858 --> 00:29:34,881
Oh?

605
00:29:34,910 --> 00:29:37,690
Earlier, I scammed someone at a restaurant.

606
00:29:37,916 --> 00:29:41,449
Ordered a ton of food.

607
00:29:42,488 --> 00:29:44,555
That’s how dumb your whole neighborhood is!

608
00:29:44,805 --> 00:29:46,065
You shameless liar!

609
00:29:46,090 --> 00:29:47,805
You scammed the
entire neighborhood!

610
00:29:48,322 --> 00:29:50,555
And why did you have to hit my face?!

611
00:29:50,865 --> 00:29:53,039
My face is my best asset!

612
00:29:53,516 --> 00:29:54,783
Well, that’s on you!

613
00:29:55,784 --> 00:29:59,727
You just had to see me! Now
you’re caught—but not locked up! O

614
00:30:01,110 --> 00:30:01,549
Ow!

615
00:30:01,574 --> 00:30:02,761
Hey, Valerie!

616
00:30:03,806 --> 00:30:04,820
Are you sure about this?!

617
00:30:05,697 --> 00:30:07,723
Let’s see what you’ve got!

618
00:30:17,913 --> 00:30:19,693
That hurt! I got a bump!

619
00:30:20,346 --> 00:30:21,399
How did you find out?!

620
00:30:21,450 --> 00:30:22,757
We got suspicious!

621
00:30:23,147 --> 00:30:24,834
You suddenly started acting different!

622
00:30:24,859 --> 00:30:29,018
Then when we realized our wallets
were missing, we knew what was up!

623
00:30:29,603 --> 00:30:31,476
That’s right! Hey, Valerie!

624
00:30:31,817 --> 00:30:35,504
Give us back our wallets—
And our ten-thousand bills!

625
00:30:35,529 --> 00:30:36,695
That was in our wallets!

626
00:30:36,781 --> 00:30:37,781
Liar!

627
00:30:38,232 --> 00:30:39,190
Liar?!

628
00:30:39,215 --> 00:30:40,601
There were only receipts in there!

629
00:30:40,633 --> 00:30:42,030
And for you, just vouchers!

630
00:30:42,055 --> 00:30:43,654
Vouchers, huh?!

631
00:30:43,900 --> 00:30:45,060
Vouchers, receipts?!

632
00:30:45,140 --> 00:30:46,030
No way!

633
00:30:46,055 --> 00:30:47,055
We don’t believe you!

634
00:30:54,519 --> 00:30:56,772
Don’t come back here, Valerie!

635
00:30:57,003 --> 00:30:58,383
- Valerie?
- Valerie.

636
00:31:00,653 --> 00:31:01,707
That hurt…

637
00:31:02,166 --> 00:31:03,240
Tso K...

638
00:31:03,605 --> 00:31:04,965
I’m really sorry, Tso K.

639
00:31:05,672 --> 00:31:06,865
So much happened.

640
00:31:07,640 --> 00:31:08,847
I even fell asleep earlier.

641
00:31:08,872 --> 00:31:11,440
Sleep?! All you do is sleep.

642
00:31:11,657 --> 00:31:13,210
Thanks, Ate Mariposa.

643
00:31:13,696 --> 00:31:15,229
Pfft! It’s nothing.

644
00:31:15,254 --> 00:31:16,280
You guys don’t need to thank me.

645
00:31:16,305 --> 00:31:19,978
You know Tso K is special to me.

646
00:31:20,850 --> 00:31:22,710
I’m the only one weak for him.

647
00:31:24,219 --> 00:31:26,146
Okay! Okay, fine!

648
00:31:27,370 --> 00:31:31,595
Now that there’s no manager
and that position is open,

649
00:31:32,276 --> 00:31:37,247
I’ve realized there’s only one
real requirement to be a manager.

650
00:31:37,514 --> 00:31:38,678
Ooooh…

651
00:31:39,082 --> 00:31:41,996
You need to be trustworthy.

652
00:31:42,246 --> 00:31:43,326
That’s right!

653
00:31:43,914 --> 00:31:46,641
And someone familiar.

654
00:31:47,439 --> 00:31:48,493
Familiar?

655
00:31:49,762 --> 00:31:50,442
Tso K...

656
00:31:50,481 --> 00:31:52,621
I’ll take that offer now!

657
00:31:52,646 --> 00:31:55,209
- Tso K! Tso K!
- Kiss, kiss!

658
00:31:58,659 --> 00:32:00,306
On the lungs, on the lungs!

659
00:32:00,331 --> 00:32:01,117
On the lungs?!

660
00:32:01,142 --> 00:32:02,608
- What is this, Iskineport?!
- Let’s just hug!

661
00:32:04,600 --> 00:32:07,146
Hug! Hug! Group hug!

662
00:32:08,083 --> 00:32:09,109
Group hug!

663
00:32:09,183 --> 00:32:10,237
Group hug!

664
00:32:12,384 --> 00:32:13,644
You shameless people!

665
00:32:13,732 --> 00:32:17,459
You’re all big and strong,
and you just left me there!

666
00:32:18,145 --> 00:32:20,138
Only Mariposa saved me!

667
00:32:20,322 --> 00:32:21,603
You pervs!

668
00:32:21,716 --> 00:32:23,443
Wow, Tso K is making wild accusations!

669
00:32:24,361 --> 00:32:25,867
Oh, now you’re all awake, huh?!

670
00:32:26,131 --> 00:32:27,918
Everyone suddenly comes out now!

671
00:32:28,596 --> 00:32:31,790
Tso K, why’d you mess
with my crutch? I’m injured!

672
00:32:31,834 --> 00:32:34,051
Want me to call Valerie? Huh?

673
00:32:34,331 --> 00:32:34,845
Go ahead!

674
00:32:34,913 --> 00:32:36,626
- Huh? You’re okay with that?
- Yes!

675
00:32:37,050 --> 00:32:39,167
I’ll call L too—

676
00:32:40,214 --> 00:32:41,420
Let’s get out of here!

677
00:32:44,496 --> 00:32:46,163
Go, go, go home!

678
00:32:46,647 --> 00:32:49,247
Iskineport, even with an
injury, you’re still fighting back!

679
00:32:49,366 --> 00:32:51,886
Thanks, really. Mariposa, I appreciate it.

680
00:32:51,911 --> 00:32:53,210
- I got you, Tso K!
- Thanks!

681
00:32:53,712 --> 00:32:55,019
You—go back to sleep!

682
00:32:56,249 --> 00:32:57,809
Oh no, what do we do now?

683
00:32:58,529 --> 00:33:00,179
We’re stuffed!

684
00:33:00,563 --> 00:33:02,943
My love, there’s no way
we can finish all this food!

685
00:33:03,031 --> 00:33:04,991
If we don’t eat it,
it’ll just go to waste!

686
00:33:05,016 --> 00:33:05,918
No way!

687
00:33:05,943 --> 00:33:07,910
That’s not a problem—

688
00:33:08,011 --> 00:33:10,064
we’ll just put everything in the fridge,

689
00:33:10,356 --> 00:33:11,909
and then when we need it…

690
00:33:11,934 --> 00:33:13,599
Come on, don’t you know this?

691
00:33:13,624 --> 00:33:16,361
You put it in the fridge, and
when you need it, you just reheat it.

692
00:33:16,386 --> 00:33:17,781
That’ll last for days, though.

693
00:33:17,806 --> 00:33:18,653
Yeah, and there’s so much!

694
00:33:18,678 --> 00:33:20,651
That’s how business
is, Atasha, Andres, right?

695
00:33:20,676 --> 00:33:24,693
I told you before, didn’t I? Sometimes
you win, sometimes you lose.

696
00:33:24,778 --> 00:33:28,041
But I still don’t regret what you guys did.

697
00:33:28,135 --> 00:33:28,862
Mmm.

698
00:33:28,887 --> 00:33:34,160
And sometimes you get lucky,
sometimes you don’t. But next time…

699
00:33:34,393 --> 00:33:34,853
Be careful!

700
00:33:34,917 --> 00:33:36,476
- …we’ll just be more careful.
- That’s right.

701
00:33:36,581 --> 00:33:37,668
- Right?
- Correct!

702
00:33:37,866 --> 00:33:38,794
You’re right, Cha.

703
00:33:38,819 --> 00:33:39,554
Hmm?

704
00:33:39,579 --> 00:33:40,625
That’s true!

705
00:33:42,608 --> 00:33:44,401
What Cha said is really true.

706
00:33:44,541 --> 00:33:47,094
It’s hard to trust people.

707
00:33:47,511 --> 00:33:49,638
And there are only a few you can really…

708
00:33:49,663 --> 00:33:50,664
Only a few what?!

709
00:33:50,689 --> 00:33:55,439
Only a few people you can truly trust, BFF.

710
00:33:55,924 --> 00:33:57,351
The ones who actually deserve it!

711
00:33:58,006 --> 00:33:59,579
Like my manager!

712
00:34:00,132 --> 00:34:01,159
I love that!

713
00:34:01,184 --> 00:34:02,096
Manager?!

714
00:34:02,121 --> 00:34:07,333
Thank you so much for the
trust, Boss K and Kuya Aga.

715
00:34:07,556 --> 00:34:11,152
Thanks a lot, but now, you
won’t lose any more money,

716
00:34:11,176 --> 00:34:14,563
because you’re lucky
to have neighbors like us.

717
00:34:14,628 --> 00:34:15,968
- Yes!
- Oh, yes!

718
00:34:15,993 --> 00:34:19,500
Wait, wait! Did I hear that right?

719
00:34:19,784 --> 00:34:22,184
Why? Why are we lucky?

720
00:34:23,039 --> 00:34:24,086
Because here’s the thing—

721
00:34:24,665 --> 00:34:26,758
we know you got scammed.

722
00:34:27,251 --> 00:34:35,182
Listen, you got scammed, and since I
almost had a bad experience myself…

723
00:34:35,207 --> 00:34:35,782
That’s right…

724
00:34:36,069 --> 00:34:40,889
I thought, why not just buy all of it?

725
00:34:40,914 --> 00:34:41,867
- What?!
- At least some of it!

726
00:34:42,511 --> 00:34:43,639
Really?!

727
00:34:43,664 --> 00:34:44,717
- I’ll buy it!
- Really?!

728
00:34:44,875 --> 00:34:45,917
Yes!

729
00:34:46,040 --> 00:34:50,366
And whatever’s left,
we’ll buy little by little.

730
00:34:50,391 --> 00:34:51,640
There you go!

731
00:34:56,451 --> 00:34:57,607
Thank you, thank you!

732
00:34:58,909 --> 00:35:00,007
There’s more, there’s more!

733
00:35:00,032 --> 00:35:01,459
A huge thank you to all of you!

734
00:35:01,550 --> 00:35:02,696
Thank you, guys!

735
00:35:02,763 --> 00:35:04,196
You really listened to me!

736
00:35:09,514 --> 00:35:10,634
- This is amazing!
- Speaking of…

737
00:35:10,684 --> 00:35:12,851
- Hey, speaking of!
- Speaking of…

738
00:35:12,876 --> 00:35:19,411
In good times and bad,
Pers is first, Pers is the star!

739
00:35:19,771 --> 00:35:24,778
Because now, in the whole
Barangay Singko, things are booming!

740
00:35:25,218 --> 00:35:27,811
Our Gen-Z friend group is complete!

741
00:35:27,836 --> 00:35:29,237
Do you know Don Al?

742
00:35:29,404 --> 00:35:30,104
Don Al Duck?

743
00:35:30,129 --> 00:35:32,050
Meet my daughter, Daphne Duck!

744
00:35:32,091 --> 00:35:33,911
Looks like Daphne has a crush on you, huh?

745
00:35:34,099 --> 00:35:35,480
I really have a crush on him.

746
00:35:35,533 --> 00:35:37,366
Why does it seem like your
eyes are getting blurrier?

747
00:35:37,426 --> 00:35:38,719
- Hi, Andres!
- Good evening!

748
00:35:40,158 --> 00:35:41,851
Oh, what happened to the lights?!

749
00:35:43,064 --> 00:35:44,751
Oh, what are you doing?!

750
00:35:44,792 --> 00:35:46,319
Oh! Caught you!

751
00:35:46,344 --> 00:35:47,763
What are you doing with my daughter?!

752
00:35:47,978 --> 00:35:49,405
Nothing! Nothing! I promise!

753
00:35:49,430 --> 00:35:51,082
Nothing?! Just look at yourselves!

754
00:35:51,218 --> 00:35:54,145
Marriage, or I’ll shut down your store!

755
00:35:54,516 --> 00:35:56,316
We got robbed.

756
00:35:57,871 --> 00:35:59,598
Muffin is really good at this, huh?!

757
00:35:59,623 --> 00:36:00,403
That’s your savings?

758
00:36:00,428 --> 00:36:01,127
- Yes.
- Yeah.

759
00:36:01,152 --> 00:36:02,266
Not stolen money?

760
00:36:02,291 --> 00:36:04,978
Are you accusing us of stealing from you?!

761
00:36:05,118 --> 00:36:06,417
I’m getting married.

762
00:36:06,442 --> 00:36:07,488
What?!

763
00:36:07,513 --> 00:36:08,757
Traitor!
